<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:50:18Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>The Cornell 7: Allegations spark fury over gang rape culture</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e7c568d46693ae9d13268e01990da48f0321d71dcdbf3bfd64955b800037ff5f</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:49:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T14:39:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261002-the-cornell-7-allegations-spark-fury-over-gang-rape-culture--c1482a18eb2c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261002-the-cornell-7-allegations-spark-fury-over-gang-rape-culture" /><summary type="html">How allegations of a gang rape at an American Ivy League university have set social media alight, sparking widespread fury over the way colleges and universities handle sexual assault cases. Also the French parliament is currently debating a major new bill aimed at tackling violence against women and children. But does it go far enough? Annette Young asks Dr Andreea Gruev-Vintila, a social psychologist who assisted with the drafting of the legislation. Plus the king of Morocco names Marrakesh mayor, Fatima Ezzahra El Mansouri, as the country's first female prime minister.</summary><category term="The 51%" /></entry><entry><title>U2 celebrate 50 years in music with surprise gigs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c5f97874b34483340eed2ab7557ab91001ebbc4563d50622e7b66c782acddfc9</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:49:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T14:12:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261002-u2-celebrate-50-years-in-music-with-surprise-gigs--a0713dc79bbb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261002-u2-celebrate-50-years-in-music-with-surprise-gigs" /><summary type="html">They could have filled a stadium or two for this golden anniversary, but U2 decided to go back to their roots and mark 50 years as a band with a few low-key gigs in their hometown of Dublin. We take a closer look.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu warns of 'very heavy price' if any country found to be behind FlyDubai incident</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c62ad91d57c123729a613207d1ba7d7b27f4d5f7ad7ad0ae38c4aa75cd70a24d</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:49:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T13:55:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261002-netanyahu-warns-of-very-heavy-price-if-any-country-found-to-be-behind-flydubai-incident--ca93f0f1308d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261002-netanyahu-warns-of-very-heavy-price-if-any-country-found-to-be-behind-flydubai-incident" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Friday warned that any country or organisation found to be responsible for the violent clash on board an Israel-bound FlyDubai flight would "pay a very heavy price". While Netanyahu has alleged the co-pilot who stabbed his captain mid-flight had undergone "Islamist radicalisation", the motive behind the incident remains unclear.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>What the media got right and wrong about Cornell gang rape case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4225ec0175c8678ef3656407015076a7965f405eaaab305d0a9b067db60b1950</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:49:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T13:53:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20261002-what-the-media-got-right-and-wrong-about-cornell-gang-rape-case--863be3ca8b9a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20261002-what-the-media-got-right-and-wrong-about-cornell-gang-rape-case" /><summary type="html">The alleged gang rape at America's Cornell University has shocked many people around the world and raised questions about institutional failure and toxic masculinity. The story was first broken by student journalists and national media soon followed, thrusting it in the spotlight. While there has been excellent reporting, the story has also exposed failures in how some pieces framed officials' statements alongside Jane Doe's allegations. We take a closer look in Scoop.</summary><category term="Scoop" /></entry><entry><title>'Apocalyptic scenes' as France school protests escalate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b1681246586e3b078278bfd4f60797a96c90995cdbf5aa80b448d8d11fc558f</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:49:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T13:42:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-apocalyptic-scenes-as-france-school-protests-escalate--0acf7e145699.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-apocalyptic-scenes-as-france-school-protests-escalate" /><summary type="html">France 24's Olivia Bizot reports from the Paris suburb of Aubervilliers, where she says protests over school conditions have left "apocalyptic" scenes in their wake. The protest movement, which began last week in the Paris region and rapidly spread nationwide, has seen teenage pupils block access to buildings and clash with police.</summary></entry><entry><title>Students and police clash as France struggles to quell school protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9d834ec2aff492f1114b56d8a5b572e59ed89829e91baa6e7fc15e1e013a4605</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:49:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T13:40:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-students-and-police-clash-as-france-struggles-to-quell-school-protests--0f4ec34f20c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-students-and-police-clash-as-france-struggles-to-quell-school-protests" /><summary type="html">Riot police clashed with high school ​students in cities across France on Friday, as President Emmanuel Macron's government battled to contain increasingly violent protests over classroom conditions and funding. The protest movement has forced the closure or disrupted education at more than 560 establishments.</summary></entry><entry><title>France school protests 'rapidly becoming out of control'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26b1c7dc9567d5bbac057d392da4abaf6e77a31be1e8a2064ed448fb9b3edcc6</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:49:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T12:55:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-france-school-protests-rapidly-becoming-out-of-control--db30099ac7cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-france-school-protests-rapidly-becoming-out-of-control" /><summary type="html">French high school students lit fires outside schools and faced off with police on Friday as a protest movement that has forced the closure or disrupted education at more than 560 establishments showed no sign of abating. France 24’s Rochelle Ferguson Bouyahi takes a look at why the students are protesting, and how the demonstrations spiraled into violence.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain housing protests rage ahead of key government vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c302f931531a6478f45a213d31c32e7493990fa5da11e41f9a71caf581d1989</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:49:29Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T12:54:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-spain-housing-protests-rage-ahead-of-key-government-vote--14ba46dba0f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-spain-housing-protests-rage-ahead-of-key-government-vote" /><summary type="html">Spanish lawmakers are due to vote on Friday on two government housing decrees drawn up after an outcry over the eviction of an 87-year-old woman, with their passage in doubt. Several hundred people held raucous protests in Madrid and other Spanish cities ahead of the vote, with demonstrators rattling keys, blowing whistles, banging spoons against pots.</summary></entry><entry><title>Paraguay, a tax and political haven for Brazil's far right</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e1742d7eebf082b418af1ce1a1804b6f0e68937e06be3b8c2be5eba7502ff36c</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:49:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T12:48:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261002-paraguay-a-tax-and-political-haven-for-brazil-s-far-right--68deff3b0c43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261002-paraguay-a-tax-and-political-haven-for-brazil-s-far-right" /><summary type="html">Over the past five years, applications for residence permits submitted by Brazilians in Paraguay have more than doubled. Many of them are Bolsonaro supporters who are afraid October's presidential election will be won by incumbent leader Lula – whom they accuse of plunging the Latin American giant into an unprecedented economic crisis. FRANCE 24's Fanny Lothaire, Valeria Saccone and Mélanie Blondeau report, with Jan Onoszko.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>What's real and what's fake? How AI is impacting Brazil's election race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e32c16118a6adeb5e22f842c344bacba063ce5c68f440c75a50e9f1ff6b430aa</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:49:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:34:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261002-what-s-real-and-what-s-fake-how-ai-is-impacting-brazil-s-election-race--0b74a4095735.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261002-what-s-real-and-what-s-fake-how-ai-is-impacting-brazil-s-election-race" /><summary type="html">With just two days to go before the first round of Brazil's presidential election, artificial intelligence is taking centre stage, whether it's a deepfake avatar of former president Jair Bolsonaro to support his son's candidacy, or an AI-generated working-class female voter criticising President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva. According to the Brazilian intelligence agency, disinformation will be one of the main challenges of this election. Our correspondents report.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>EU ‘fully rejects’ US threat to ban diesel exports unless bloc releases more fuel stocks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09727b1f5cf14ccd86aa850550a46aa99918e6141bedda0e1ef2f4ce3813d752</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:49:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:15:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261002-eu-fully-rejects-us-threat-to-ban-diesel-exports-unless-bloc-releases-more-fuel-stocks--df4aae889a92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261002-eu-fully-rejects-us-threat-to-ban-diesel-exports-unless-bloc-releases-more-fuel-stocks" /><summary type="html">The European Union on Friday pushed back against a US threat to ban any diesel exports unless the 27-member bloc releases more of its fuel stocks, “fully” rejecting the move, an EU official said. French President Emmanuel Macron will chair a video call with his G7 counterparts Friday to discuss possible measures on global fuel markets.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's election: Lula or Bolsonaro Jr?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:05201d18ec28557886853119e5326250b7d8954fcf2304c5f4b77a9933a632ba</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:49:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:04:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261002-brazil-s-election-lula-or-bolsonaro-jr--90417820582f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261002-brazil-s-election-lula-or-bolsonaro-jr" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Friday, October 2: We look at reactions in the French papers after high school blockades turned violent across France. We also look ahead to Brazil's two-round presidential election, which begins this weekend. The electoral campaign culminated with the cancellation of a presidential debate after both President Lula and his rival Flavio Bolsonaro pulled out. Finally, this year's Comedy Wildlife Awards finalists do not disappoint.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria rolls out digital postcodes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46eb05dda6741cc27e6894607f54d1f0e4d0f9cfed60e182949e585c77bc4b75</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:49:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T10:55:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-nigeria-rolls-out-digital-postcodes--17c7e3624d39.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-nigeria-rolls-out-digital-postcodes" /><summary type="html">Nigeria’s Postal Service has launched a National Digital Alphanumeric Postcode System. The system is designed to help Nigerians find the postcodes of locations across the country. Before now, house identification in Nigeria was based on an unreliable house numbering system. Locating places was difficult, time consuming and sometimes even expensive. But there may challenges using the new system in a country with poor urban planning and illegal building constructions.</summary></entry><entry><title>Eritrea cuts ties with Ethiopia over embassy closure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cbf6695e55aa9c63a86000c3c17c5c91c0880ea22ae7cb2eb07bc4e6686c5a4c</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:49:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T10:54:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-eritrea-cuts-ties-with-ethiopia-over-embassy-closure--144dd1fd5336.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-eritrea-cuts-ties-with-ethiopia-over-embassy-closure" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia ordered the closure of its embassy in Eritrea and declared 10 Eritrean diplomats persona non grata on Thursday, prompting Asmara to sever all diplomatic ties with its neighbour after overnight blasts heard in Addis Ababa sparked fears about renewed conflict in northern Ethiopia spreading. France 24's Tom Canetti has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why Brazil's gun lobby is backing Bolsonaro as country heads to polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c4b5efc0012b43a6da9842e1f150978e70c3132d591b56a918b86e8fbd46d34</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:49:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T10:19:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-why-brazil-s-gun-lobby-is-backing-bolsonaro-as-country-heads-to-polls--dc9439570d9e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-why-brazil-s-gun-lobby-is-backing-bolsonaro-as-country-heads-to-polls" /><summary type="html">As Brazil heads to the polls, one issue that could influence votes particularly in the rural south is access to firearms. Under Jair Bolsonaro, Brazil became more heavily armed than ever before: the number of registered hunters, shooters and collectors – known by the acronym ‘CACs’ – increased sevenfold in four years. Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva promised to reverse this trend, much to the irritation of the powerful gun lobby. France 24’s team in Brazil sent this report.</summary></entry><entry><title>'America is leaving Iraq, but Iran isn't: Withdrawal a massive strategic and tactical mistake'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5a76594cc0185bcfffa198c58e80de6066a7423e523fe8edfc6fb17c628788c</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:49:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T10:11:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-america-is-leaving-iraq-but-iran-isn-t-withdrawal-a-massive-strategic-and-tactical-mistake---0b781c6b753d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-america-is-leaving-iraq-but-iran-isn-t-withdrawal-a-massive-strategic-and-tactical-mistake-1" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Bamo Nouri, investigative journalist and also Honorary Research Fellow with the Department of International Politics at City Saint George's University of London. He sees the end of the American military presence in Iraq as a profound shift in the balance of power inside the country. For him, the central question is not whether Iraq has formally regained sovereignty, but whether it possesses the political cohesion, security capacity and economic independence necessary to exercise that sovereignty.</summary></entry><entry><title>Amid French school protests, students seek 'respect, dignity and decent working conditions'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da36a25640d80d585b91a5d0b67029669bbf7afe1c1a023b28e19375881fa502</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:49:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T10:02:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/amid-french-school-protests-students-seek-respect-dignity-and-decent-working-conditions--7d9da3408af7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/amid-french-school-protests-students-seek-respect-dignity-and-decent-working-conditions" /><summary type="html">Alison Sargent is pleased to welcome Éric Fassin, a sociologist and professor at Paris VIII University. He sees these student protests first and foremost as a demand for equality, dignity and recognition. Students from working-class suburbs are asking for the basic conditions that make studying possible and, ultimately, the same opportunities as students elsewhere. What began among students in the Parisian suburbs has spread, but its fundamental meaning remains the same: this is a social movement with a political and democratic dimension. He also see these protests in the context of a longer history of repression of social movements in France.</summary></entry><entry><title>As Europe's balance of power shifts eastward, France &amp; Spain seek to 'reinforce their own positions'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bdc08d80afae64c97223c2fddc9ea37d2da8d997c2f5b23362ffaf7411f5c94b</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:50:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T09:49:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-as-europe-s-balance-of-power-shifts-eastward-france-spain-seek-to-reinforce-their-own-posit--c379b49194e6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-as-europe-s-balance-of-power-shifts-eastward-france-spain-seek-to-reinforce-their-own-positions-1" /><summary type="html">Delano D'Souza is pleased to welcome Carlos Mascarell Vilar, political scientist based in Spain. From his own perspective, Emmanuel Macron's visit to Spain needs to be understood by European power, political legacy, and geoeconomics. France and Spain are seeking to reinforce their bilateral relationship at a moment when the balance of power within Europe is changing rapidly, particularly with the growing importance of countries in the east such as Poland. For Macron, strengthening the Madrid-Paris axis is also part of a broader effort to advance European defence and strategic sovereignty.</summary></entry><entry><title>Matisse comes to Amsterdam in major new show</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd2207d0e6b6e5a42f5cc9ced0d9f2dedcbb5e936743e8ec22490bdc2e1fa559</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:50:02Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T09:48:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-matisse-comes-to-amsterdam-in-major-new-show--fb8818036a45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-matisse-comes-to-amsterdam-in-major-new-show" /><summary type="html">From the October 3 visitors to Amsterdam's H'ART museum will be able to see an extensive collection of works by artist Henri Matisse alongside pieces inspired by his legacy, including Mark Rothko, Barnett Newman, and Pablo Picasso. The new exhibition was organised in collaboration with the Pompidou Centre in Paris.</summary></entry><entry><title>Lula and Bolsonaro in dead heat as Brazil goes to polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:837e0fc3e1680030d7b6af6d9905e070acaffab09ebbee8fe6261a5823243b80</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:50:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T09:47:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-lula-and-bolsonaro-in-dead-heat-as-brazil-goes-to-polls--9790bd336f59.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-lula-and-bolsonaro-in-dead-heat-as-brazil-goes-to-polls" /><summary type="html">Brazilian presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro on Thursday bowed out of the final debate ahead of elections pitting him against leader Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva, who also declined to attend. Lula, on the cusp of 81, will face off against the son of ex-leader Jair Bolsonaro in a first-round vote on Sunday, with polls giving him a slight advantage. The pair are neck-and-neck in projections for a potential runoff on October 25, however.</summary></entry><entry><title>French pensioners set to feel pinch under belt-tightening budget</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77c0b791f6ed7d5da6a76ae7de80bef1d3e097da8ad57f178ef5629a83c8d057</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:50:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T09:34:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-french-pensioners-set-to-feel-pinch-under-belt-tightening-budget--1719d750eb41.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-french-pensioners-set-to-feel-pinch-under-belt-tightening-budget" /><summary type="html">French pensioners will be among those expected to contribute to balancing the government's books, according to the 2027 draft budget unveiled on Thursday. Pensions exceeding 1,260 euros per month will be partially frozen and the cap on the 10% income tax deduction will be lowered, measures that received mixed reactions from pensioners.</summary></entry><entry><title>French website publishes evidence for antisemitism claims against Bardella</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae35eda5e24dd95ad2088b3f9134135e259b14b4ed596a5a451f8d38bc066dd8</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:50:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T09:27:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-french-website-publishes-evidence-for-antisemitism-claims-against-bardella--e28f2cc49f88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-french-website-publishes-evidence-for-antisemitism-claims-against-bardella" /><summary type="html">French investigative journalism website Mediapart said Thursday it had been able to authenticate antisemitic messages from 2013 attributed to far-right presidential candidate Marine Le Pen's de facto deputy Jordan Bardella. The allegations come just seven months out from the election where voters will choose a replacement for President Emmanuel Macron, with Le Pen leading opinion polls.</summary></entry><entry><title>France closes 400 high schools as teens protests escalate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c2da560681baed9f63037e00fd864019d2f1845c16c7744e6d29c6ed0d85cc2</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:50:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T09:11:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-france-closes-400-high-schools-as-teens-protests-escalate--59ca5c46206e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-france-closes-400-high-schools-as-teens-protests-escalate" /><summary type="html">Almost 400 high schools were closed across France on Friday over a week-long protest movement by pupils over inadequate conditions at schools including overheated classrooms and a lack of teachers. The protests have seen students clash with police with some 2,000 people arrested, with pupils also blocking access to schools. France 24’s Olivia Bizot reports from outside a high school near Paris where she says many protesters are also decrying what they says is the use of police violence.</summary></entry><entry><title>Can AI play a role in reducing inequality?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a515c811af6c3bafde74c85df3ba3141ecead00be247ff3af8d696aba1ca492e</id><updated>2026-10-02T14:50:18Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T09:06:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20261002-can-ai-play-a-role-in-reducing-inequality--9b82314c447c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/people-profit/20261002-can-ai-play-a-role-in-reducing-inequality" /><summary type="html">In the debate about how best to regulate artificial intelligence, what about its role in development and aid? Warnings about the potential for exacerbating inequality are rife – but the World Bank argues that the technology could be harnessed for good.</summary><category term="People &amp; Profit" /></entry></feed>
